## 📄 Complete `.npmrc` Templates

### ✅ Project-level `.npmrc` (Recommended)
> Save as `.npmrc` in your project root → **add to .gitignore** so token never gets committed
```ini
# Use GitHub Packages registry for your scoped packages
@YOUR_USERNAME:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# Authenticate to GitHub Packages via environment variable
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
```

### ✅ Global `~/.npmrc` (For all projects on your machine)
> Replace `YOUR_TOKEN` with your real PAT once — works everywhere
```ini
@YOUR_USERNAME:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=ghp_YOUR_REAL_TOKEN_HERE
```

---

## ⚙️ GitHub Actions Workflow (Full Example)

> Save to: `.github/workflows/npm-publish.yml`
```yaml
name: Publish Package to GitHub Packages

on:
  release:
    types: [created]   # Auto-publish when you create a new Release
  push:
    branches: [main]  # Optional: also publish on push to main

jobs:
  publish:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    permissions:
      contents: read
      packages: write   # Required for publishing to GitHub Packages

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          registry-url: 'https://npm.pkg.github.com'

      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm ci

      - name: Build package
        run: npm run build

      - name: Publish to GitHub Packages
        run: npm publish
        env:
          NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
```

### Key points about this workflow:
- ✅ **No manual token needed** — `GITHUB_TOKEN` is auto-provided by Actions
- ✅ Permissions set correctly (`packages: write`)
- ✅ Auto-publish on new Release (best practice for versioning)
- ✅ Uses `npm ci` for deterministic builds

---

## 📋 `package.json` Requirements
Your package **must** be scoped to match the registry owner:
```json
{
  "name": "@your-username/your-package-name",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "publishConfig": {
    "registry": "https://npm.pkg.github.com"
  }
}
```

---

## 🚀 Usage Cheat Sheet

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Install locally (env var) | `GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx npm install` |
| Publish locally (env var) | `GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx npm publish` |
| Install from Actions | Auto-handled by workflow above |

---

## 🔐 Security Checklist
- [ ] `.npmrc` is in `.gitignore`
- [ ] Token has **minimum required scopes**: `repo`, `write:packages`, `read:packages`
- [ ] Using `${GITHUB_TOKEN}` env var in committed `.npmrc` (never hardcode token)
- [ ] `package.json` name matches scope: `@owner/package-name`

